{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795770848,"nonce":"j1TLlNsQuhINJzuBj0ccfcZ91YY=","title":"Coloured box shadows are drawn darker than their colour","message":"A shadow of 0 0 20px #b8bcb5 on white draws (181,182,180) just outside the box, where the CSS model gives about (221,223,220). Black shadows look right, so theme shadows hide it.\n\nThe shadow, circle shadow, inline shadow and notch shadow paths multiply the whole shadow colour by the falloff, and the pipelines blend straight alpha, so the colour is scaled by the falloff twice. Only the alpha may carry the falloff.\n\nFound checking that the default theme keeps a user's shadows (GitHub #86).","files":null}]}